    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "# Terms of Use\n\nEffective Date: June 12, 2026\n\nThese Terms of Use (\"Terms\") govern your access to and use of Arrow Out: Line Master Pro, including any related mobile applications, websites, features, content, services, and support channels (collectively, the \"Game\"). The Game is provided by SAILA IMPEX (\"Company\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\").\n\nBy downloading, installing, accessing, or using the Game, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Game.\n\n## 1. Eligibility\n\nYou must be at least 13 years old, or the minimum age required in your country or region, to use the Game. If you are under the age of legal majority where you live, you may use the Game only with permission from a parent or legal guardian.\n\nThe Game is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. If your game is directed to children or listed in a family or kids category, replace this section with terms that match your actual age rating, parental consent flow, and applicable children's privacy requirements.\n\n## 2. License to Use the Game\n\nSubject to your compliance with these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to download, install, and use the Game for your personal, non-commercial entertainment purposes.\n\nYou do not acquire ownership of the Game, any content in the Game, or any related intellectual property rights. All rights not expressly granted to you are reserved by us and our licensors.\n\n## 3. Accounts and Device Access\n\nThe Game may allow you to play without creating an account. Some features may require device permissions, platform services, or third-party services, such as cloud saves, advertising identifiers, analytics, push notifications, or in-app purchases.\n\nYou are responsible for maintaining control of your device, platform account, and any credentials used to access the Game. We are not responsible for losses caused by unauthorized access to your device or platform account unless required by applicable law.\n\n## 4. Acceptable Use\n\nYou agree not to:\n\n- Use the Game for any unlawful, harmful, fraudulent, abusive, or unauthorized purpose.\n- Cheat, exploit bugs, manipulate gameplay, use bots, scripts, automation, emulators, modified clients, or unauthorized third-party tools.\n- Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, modify, copy, distribute, sell, lease, sublicense, or create derivative works from the Game, except where applicable law expressly allows it.\n- Interfere with, overload, disrupt, or attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Game, our systems, or third-party systems.\n- Circumvent security, payment, advertising, analytics, or access-control features.\n- Use the Game to infringe intellectual property, privacy, publicity, or other rights.\n- Harass, threaten, impersonate, or harm other users, our staff, or third parties.\n\nWe may suspend or terminate access to the Game if we believe you have violated these Terms, harmed the Game, or created legal, security, or operational risk.\n\n## 5. Virtual Items, Rewards, and In-App Purchases\n\nThe Game may include virtual currency, virtual items, boosters, lives, rewards, skins, subscriptions, or other digital content (\"Virtual Items\"). Virtual Items are licensed, not sold. They have no real-world cash value, are not redeemable for money or property, and cannot be transferred outside the Game unless we expressly allow it.\n\nPrices, availability, features, rewards, and Virtual Item balances may change at any time, subject to applicable law and platform rules. We may modify, rebalance, remove, or discontinue Virtual Items or gameplay features as part of operating and improving the Game.\n\nPurchases are processed by the app store or platform through which you downloaded the Game, such as Apple App Store or Google Play. Refund requests are handled according to the applicable platform's refund policies, unless applicable law requires otherwise.\n\n## 6. Advertising and Third-Party Services\n\nThe Game may display ads, including rewarded ads, interstitial ads, banner ads, or personalized ads where permitted. Ads may be provided by third-party advertising networks and mediation partners. These partners may collect or receive device identifiers, advertising identifiers, approximate location inferred from IP address, gameplay events, ad interactions, and other data as described in our Privacy Policy.\n\nThird-party services are governed by their own terms and privacy policies. We are not responsible for third-party content, websites, services, ads, offers, or purchase flows.\n\n## 7. Push Notifications\n\nIf enabled, the Game may send push notifications about gameplay reminders, rewards, updates, events, offers, or service messages. You can disable push notifications through your device settings at any time.\n\n## 8. User Content\n\nIf the Game allows you to submit names, messages, profile information, feedback, support requests, images, or other content (\"User Content\"), you are responsible for that content. You grant us a worldwide, royalty-free, sublicensable, transferable license to host, store, reproduce, modify, display, publish, translate, and use User Content for operating, improving, promoting, and supporting the Game.\n\nYou must not submit User Content that is illegal, abusive, misleading, infringing, obscene, hateful, or harmful. We may remove or restrict User Content at any time.\n\nIf the Game does not include user-generated content, you may remove this section before publishing.\n\n## 9. Updates and Availability\n\nWe may update, patch, modify, suspend, or discontinue the Game, features, content, events, rewards, or services at any time. Some updates may be required to continue using the Game.\n\nWe do not guarantee that the Game will be available at all times, error-free, secure, or compatible with every device, operating system, network, or region.\n\n## 10. Intellectual Property\n\nThe Game, including software, artwork, characters, levels, designs, names, logos, music, sounds, text, user interface, animations, gameplay systems, databases, and other content, is owned by us or our licensors and is protected by intellectual property and other laws.\n\nYou may not use our names, logos, trademarks, or game assets without our prior written permission, except as allowed by law.\n\n## 11. Feedback\n\nIf you send us suggestions, ideas, bug reports, comments, or other feedback, you grant us the right to use them without restriction or compensation to you.\n\n## 12. Privacy\n\nYour use of the Game is also governed by our Privacy Policy, which explains how we collect, use, share, and protect information. Please review it carefully.\n\n## 13. Disclaimers\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, the Game is provided \"as is\" and \"as available\" without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, non-infringement, availability, accuracy, or uninterrupted operation.\n\nSome jurisdictions do not allow certain disclaimers, so some of the above may not apply to you.\n\n## 14. Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, we and our affiliates, officers, employees, contractors, partners, licensors, and service providers will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for loss of profits, data, goodwill, device functionality, or Virtual Items, arising from or related to your use of the Game.\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability for all claims related to the Game or these Terms will not exceed the greater of: (a) the amount you paid to us for the Game during the six months before the claim arose; or (b) USD $100.\n\nNothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law.\n\n## 15. Indemnity\n\nTo the extent permitted by law, you agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless us and our affiliates, officers, employees, contractors, partners, licensors, and service providers from any claims, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, and expenses, including reasonable attorneys' fees, arising from or related to your violation of these Terms, misuse of the Game, User Content, or violation of any law or third-party rights.\n\n## 16. Termination\n\nYou may stop using the Game at any time. We may suspend, restrict, or terminate your access to the Game if you violate these Terms, create risk or possible legal exposure, misuse the Game, or if we discontinue the Game.\n\nUpon termination, your license to use the Game ends immediately. Sections that by their nature should survive termination will survive, including intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability, indemnity, governing law, and dispute resolution.\n\n## 17. Governing Law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law principles, except where local consumer protection law requires otherwise.\n\nIf you operate in multiple countries or states, ask legal counsel to confirm the correct governing law, venue, consumer rights, arbitration, and class-action language.\n\n## 18. Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we will provide notice as required by applicable law, such as by updating the Effective Date, posting a notice in the Game, or using another reasonable method.\n\nYour continued use of the Game after the updated Terms become effective means you accept the updated Terms.\n\n## 19. Contact Us\n\nIf you have questions about these Terms, contact us at:\n\nSAILA IMPEX  \nD-U-N-S: 913918010  \nD.NO-8-3-167/A/4, PLOT NO.4, GROUND FLOOR  \nVIKASPURI COLONY NEAR AG COLONY  \nHyderabad - 500038  \nEmail: kartaki1988@gmail.com  \nWebsite: [WEBSITE URL]\n"
